# --- shipped ---------------------------------------------------------------
# bin/ffmpeg and bin/ffprobe are tracked: src/lib/paths.js calls them by path on
# every render. 76 MB each, under GitHub's 100 MB file cap.
# assets/fonts, vendor/lemo-opuscar (audio synth) and package-lock.json are tracked too.

# --- not shipped: not used by the reel pipeline -----------------------------
# bin/piper + bin/yt-dlp: text-to-speech and downloads. Nobody speaks in these
# reels (AGENTS.md), so neither binary is on the render path.
bin/piper/
bin/yt-dlp
# voices/: Piper .onnx models, 63–78 MB each. Same reason.
voices/
# tools/: whisper.cpp (700 MB binary + 640 MB models), Remotion, HyperFrames.
# Editing helpers, not render dependencies — see VIDEO-TOOLKIT.md to re-fetch.
tools/
# .cache/: a second copy of the same static FFmpeg build.
.cache/

# --- local scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
.tmp/
node_modules/
.playwright-mcp/
ig-*.png
yt-*.png

# --- rendered media --------------------------------------------------------
# It lives on YouTube/Instagram, and it is 400 MB of git history. The notes,
# subtitles and manifests stay.
out/**/*.mp4
out/**/*.mp3
out/**/*.jpg
out/**/*.png
out/**/*.html

# python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
